  'T/P exp' = d/B exactly, since h+I0 = alpha.  So the trivial bound overshoots by 2^d
  and the target needs a relative discrepancy saving of 2^{-d} (times poly) -- which is
  exactly the power saving named in ShellWeyl.weylBound_of_pointwise.

  Square-root cancellation gives relative discrepancy 2^{-h*kappa*B/2}; it suffices iff
  h*kappa/2 > alpha*kappa - 1, i.e. kappa < 1/(alpha - h/2):
     1/(alpha - h/2) = 1.201720
